('short-stories-1-1-1', 'The Dark', 1, 1, 1, 'short-stories', '<p>It’s the first anniversary of our marriage. My wife and I decided to go on a trip to the charming coastal city of Pondicherry. And here we are en route to Pondy Marina Beach, riding on a lovely Vespa we rented for the trip. I have a passion for photography, and so my wife is riding the Vespa while I capture the captivating beauty of every corner of this city of love.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This beach is so unique. It’s just a few steps away from the lighthouse. And right behind the lighthouse is a graveyard. The roads are so curvy. These winding roads make every street so photogenic and especially the lighthouse street. I tried to capture a shot but couldn’t get it quite right.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>My wife started rushing me to the beach as it was already getting so late. She parked the Vespa on the beachside parking lot and we started roaming on the beach holding our hands together with AR Rahman Love Melodies playing on our speakers in the background.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It’s 12.30 AM. The sky is so clear with all the stars shining together to form constellations like birds flying over space. Gazing at the shining stars, lying freely on the beach at midnight, listening to the silent waves, feeling the cool breeze, and laughing at her silly jokes. Could this day get any better?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>“Thump!”, Sound of a loud thunder.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Just as I felt good about something, suddenly the sky started getting so dark.I couldn’t see the dazzling stars any more. Surprisingly, The street lights went off too. It’s like the world went dark. What is happening? Is this it? I’m just in my 30s. I am not ready to see the end of the world so soon.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To make it even more spooky, I started hearing some weird sounds from the above like an alien invasion or something. Oh my god! Where is Rupa?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>“Rupa, Where are you?”, I screamed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I panicked just as I realized my wife Rupa was missing. All of a sudden, I started feeling a lot of weight pulling me down to the ground. I couldn\\\'t move, speak, or even think. I am losing my mind. I feel so dizzy and light-headed. It’s like I’m floating upwards into an alien UFO.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>“Isn’t it magnificent? Manu? Manu. Are you sleeping? Come on. On our vacation? Wake up Manu!”, my wife yelled.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I opened my eyes to find Rupa looking at me, relieved to see me awake. What? I’m sleeping? I rubbed my eyes firmly and opened them to find that everything is alright and it’s just a dark dream and not the dark dystopian end of the world. I had been dreaming the entire time, and it was just my mind playing tricks on me. We laughed it off, but the memory of that dream stayed with me for a long time.</p>', '2023-03-17 03:03:30', NULL),
('short-stories-1-2-1', 'The Shattered Glass: A story of blood, anger and grief', 1, 1, 2, 'short-stories', '<p>Manu, the elder brother, was sleeping in his bedroom.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It was 9 AM when he heard his mother screaming for him and his younger brother Kiran to help.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\\\"Manu! Kiran!\\\"&nbsp; Screamed his mother, \\\"Come here fast.\\\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Their 75 year old grandfather, who had been bedridden for almost two months due to filaria and elephantiasis, had slipped from his bed and was mumbling incoherently. Manu\\\'s mother, Kiran, and their grandfather\\\'s caretaker were already there, trying to lift him up as he was too heavy due to his condition. Manu joined them to help him lift and they rested him back on the bed.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Manu immediately called for an ambulance as his grandfather was sweating heavily and struggling to breathe. The ambulance service connected him to a driver and he is 20 km away and it takes at least 40 minutes to reach their location.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Meanwhile, Manu\\\'s mother gave his grandfather some hot water to help him feel better. He is so sick that he couldn’t even take solid foods. His mother or the caretaker had to feed him the juices from the food for the past few days.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The ambulance finally arrived after 50 minutes. The driver brought a stretcher and they all lifted his grandfather and placed him on it. Manu\\\'s mother and brother got into the ambulance, and he followed them on his bike.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>They admitted him to a hospital in Rajahmundry. This is the same hospital where they frequently take him for medical treatment. In fact, their grandfather just got discharged from the same hospital a few weeks ago. Manu informed the receptionist that his grandfather was in an emergency and needed a doctor right away.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The doctor checked his grandfather and found that his digestive system was completely damaged, especially his food pipe. His blood levels were too low, and the doctor prescribed two units of blood, which they had to obtain from a blood bank in Rajahmundry.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Manu started for the blood bank as soon as the doctor handed him the prescription. It took him some time to find the blood bank as the roads were too confusing. On his way, he is very terrified about his grandfather and prayed to God that nothing should happen to him.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>He finally found the \\\"Godavari Blood Bank\\\", a two-story building near the round park among very clumsy buildings. He went to the reception and they asked him to go to the lab on the first floor. He climbed the narrow, spiral stairs to the lab. Few people are waiting in line to get blood for their friend who was in an accident. They got a broker who just found a donor for them. So he had to wait until they leave.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In a long, dark room filled with blood, this technician seemed like a psychopath. OMG! It is quite scary. The technician looked at him and gave him a sinister smile, making him feel even more uncomfortable. He tried to remain calm and focused on the task at hand, hoping that he could finish quickly and leave the room as soon as possible.</p><p>***</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Technician: How may I help you sir?</p><p>Manu: Yes. My grandfather is in urgent need of two units of blood.</p><p>Technician: Sure. Do you have a prescription?</p><p>Manu: Yes. Here it is.</p><p>Technician: I see. For Surya Multispeciality Hospitals. Alright. Did you bring a donor with you?</p><p>Manu: Donor? No.</p><p>Technician: Get a donor as soon as possible and pay&nbsp;<strong>₹</strong>1,500/unit at the reception to get the blood needed.</p><p>Manu: What? No. We don\\\'t have a donor and we can\\\'t find one now. My grandfather is in an emergency.</p><p>Technician: Sorry sir. We can\\\'t give you blood unless you bring a donor. Don\\\'t worry. The donor doesn\\\'t necessarily have to be of the same blood group as the patient.</p><p>Manu: Oh, ok. Let me come back again.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\\\"What? I don\\\'t understand. My grandfather is in an emergency and needs blood right away. And the blood bank refuses to give blood until we get a donor? This doesn\\\'t make any sense at all\\\", Manu muses furiously.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As the blood bank refused to give them blood without a donor, he walked out of the diagnostic center and called his friends and relatives to find out if anyone was willing to donate blood. No luck yet. None of them were ready. Manu, his mother, and his brother had the same blood group as their grandfather, A+ve. But they had just recently recovered from COVID-19 and were ineligible to donate.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It\\\'s 2 PM and he\\\'s been waiting there for almost 2 hours searching for the donors. He was so confused and didn’t know what to do. He forwarded messages to all his WhatsApp groups. He never responded to or forwarded any such messages before. He never thought he would be in such a situation. But here he was, desperately searching for donors for his grandfather.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>In the meantime, Mahesh, Manu\\\'s friend, finally agreed to donate. He came to the blood bank and got tested. They rejected him as he was on medication for some hair treatment. Luckily, Mahesh found his friend willing to donate his blood and he too came over. Turns out he is underweight and ineligible.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>“It\\\'s better to check with other blood banks too”, suggested Mahesh.</p><p>They both went to check with other blood banks and all of them refused to give blood as the prescription is given specifically to “Godavari Blood Bank” and is invalid elsewhere. So they returned to the hospital to get the prescription. The doctor had just left for lunch and it might take at least one hour for him to be back. Manu was so tired and hungry. So they stopped at a place to eat idly.</p><p>After several unsuccessful attempts to find a donor, Manu\\\'s father contacted another blood bank that was willing to give blood without a donor. His father shared their location and contact details.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>“God dammit! What is happening? They are not at all lifting the call“, shouted Manu.</p><p>They didn\\\'t pick up the calls and didn\\\'t respond to the messages either. They went to the location to find out the blood bank was relocated to some other location and they couldn’t find it. So they came back to Godavari Blood Bank again to request them to give blood now and they would bring the donor later. Unsurprisingly, they didn’t agree and asked to bring at least one donor now and can bring another donor later for the other unit of blood .&nbsp;</p><p>It’s 5 PM and finally Manu received a call from one of his relatives, who informed him that her friend was willing to donate blood. However, it would take some time for him as he has to come from Tanuku which is 40 KM away from Rajahmundry.</p><p>Meanwhile he received another call from someone willing to donate blood. They reached the blood bank in half an hour. Luckily everything was fine and he passed all the tests. Their luck was here to stab them again and it turns out he too just recovered from COVID-19. Manu had no other option left but to wait for his aunt’s friend or until someone else is willing to donate.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Finally his aunt’s friend Bharat Kumar arrived at the blood bank at 7 PM. He passed all the tests and was ready to donate blood. Manu was so relieved. Mahesh left the blood bank as Manu finally found a donor. The technician took Bharat inside the lab and Bharat came out after 10 minutes with an apple and ORS in his hand.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The technician gave Manu a receipt to pay the bill. He rushed to the reception downstairs, paid it off and came back to get the blood from the lab. After many hours of struggle to get blood for his grandfather he is ready to leave the blood bank. He reached the hospital at 8:30 PM and handed over the blood to their nurse. He went to see his grandfather. He was sleeping. He informed his mother he was going back home and left the hospital.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Manu returned to his house and was so hungry. He was relieved that everything would be alright now as he delivered the blood needed. His mother\\\'s elder sister, Peddamma, was waiting at their home, and Manu told her that everything was fine.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As he settled down in his room and turned on his laptop, he saw a lot of messages from his internship manager. Feeling tired, he ignored them and instead called his college friend and project mate, Neeraj, to tell him about everything that had happened that day.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Suddenly, there was a scream from his aunt.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>“Ayyo! Manu!” His Peddamma screamed. “Taatha chanipoyarantaraa”</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>She cried out that Manu\\\'s grandfather had passed away.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Manu was shocked and said, “What? No! It can’t be true I just delivered the blood and came home.”&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Manu couldn\\\'t believe that his grandfather was gone. He had just given the blood to the nurse and returned home. His aunt was on a call with his mother, who confirmed that his grandfather had indeed passed away.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Manu was overwhelmed with anger. He felt that his grandfather had died just because he couldn\\\'t get the blood on time, and the blood bank was to blame. He pushed the entrance door forcefully and started his bike to the hospital. On his way, he screamed out to God, blaming everyone for his grandfather\\\'s death.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As he rode aggressively, he didn\\\'t care about any bumps on the road. He was so focused on getting to the hospital that he didn\\\'t realize the danger he was putting himself in. However, he soon regained his senses and drove more carefully, thinking about his mother and how devastated she would be if anything happened to him.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>As he approached the hospital, he imagined himself thrashing all the windows of the blood bank and beating the psychopath technician to death. However, it was too late to do anything as it was already 10 PM, and no one would be there.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>He turned towards the hospital and arrived at the entrance with his bike. The door was half open, and he ran into it so rashly that the door broke and the glass shattered all over the place. Manu got off his bike and started screaming at the nurse and security, blaming them for his grandfather\\\'s death.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>\\\"Champesaru kada ra. Andaru kalisi maa taatha ni champesaru kada ra\\\"&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>He took the keys from his bike, left the bike in the middle of the hospital hall then rushed to his grandfather\\\'s room, but it was too late. His grandfather had passed away, and Manu couldn\\\'t believe it. Manu was bleeding a little from the injuries caused by the broken glass, but his mother cleaned it up for him.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It turned out that his grandfather couldn\\\'t bear the pressure from the blood transfusion, and all his body fluids started coming out from his mouth and nose. Manu was devastated to find his grandfather dead.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', '2023-03-17 05:31:54', '2023-06-04 05:42:07'),
('streaktracker-1-1-1', 'StreakTracker - Streak & Reward', 1, 1, 1, 'streaktracker', '<h4><a href=\\\"https://streaktracker.netlify.app/\\\"><strong>StreakTracker</strong> - A Tool for Achieving Your Goals</a></h4><p>Are you struggling to stick to your daily goals and habits? Do you find it hard to maintain your motivation and focus? Then, <strong>StreakTracker</strong> is the solution you have been looking for.</p><p><strong>StreakTracker</strong> is a simple and effective tool that helps you track your progress and stay motivated as you work towards your goals. It is designed to help you maintain a consistent routine by setting a target amount and a daily reward. If you miss a day, your streak resets and you have to start over again. This approach encourages you to stay focused and committed to your goals, as you strive to maintain your streak and reach your target amount.</p><p>The tool is incredibly versatile and can be used for a variety of goals and habits, such as studying for exams, maintaining a healthy lifestyle, or learning a new skill. For instance, if you are preparing for IIT-JEE, you can set a goal to study for a certain number of hours each day and track your progress using <strong>StreakTracker</strong>. You can also set a reward for yourself, such as watching a movie or playing video games, to keep you motivated.</p><p>Similarly, software developers can use <strong>StreakTracker</strong> to track their progress and maintain their motivation as they work on their projects. By setting a goal to complete a certain number of tasks each day, you can use StreakTracker to keep yourself accountable and stay on track. The tool can also be integrated with your online learning platform, allowing you to track your progress and receive feedback on your performance.</p><p>Another area where <strong>StreakTracker</strong> can be useful is in promoting healthy eating habits. You can set a goal to eat a certain number of fruits and vegetables each day and track your progress using <strong>StreakTracker</strong>. This will help you maintain a healthy diet and ensure that you are getting the nutrients you need to stay healthy.<br><br><br>&nbsp;</p><h4>How to use <strong>StreakTracker</strong>?</h4><p>Here is the link to <strong>StreakTracker</strong></p><p><a href=\\\"https://streaktracker.netlify.app/\\\"><strong>https://streaktracker.netlify.app/</strong></a></p><p><strong>For Students:</strong></p><p>If you are a student, you can use <strong>StreakTracker</strong> to help you stay on track with your studies. For example, you can set a goal to study for a certain amount of time each day and give yourself a reward for achieving this goal. If you miss a day, you will have to start your streak over again, which will motivate you to stay on track.</p><p><strong>For Software Developers:</strong></p><p>If you are a software developer, you can use <strong>StreakTracker</strong> to help you stay motivated and achieve your coding goals. For example, you can set a goal to write a certain number of lines of code each day and give yourself a reward for achieving this goal. If you miss a day, you will have to start your streak over again, which will motivate you to stay on track.</p><p><strong>For Eating Habits:</strong></p><p>If you are looking to improve your eating habits, you can use <strong>StreakTracker</strong> to help you stay on track. For example, you can set a goal to eat a healthy meal each day and give yourself a reward for achieving this goal. If you miss a day, you will have to start your streak over again, which will motivate you to stay on track.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Conclusion</strong></p><p><strong>StreakTracker</strong> is a powerful tool that can help you achieve your goals and build positive habits. Whether you are a student, a software developer, or simply someone looking to improve their eating habits, <strong>StreakTracker</strong> can help you stay motivated and achieve your goals. So why not give it a try today and see how it can help you build the habits you need to achieve your goals!</p>', '2025-01-01 10:09:49', '2023-03-10 11:05:04');

